WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Creamy Cilantro Chipotle Chicken. 40 min · 4 servings · Mexican

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Ingredients: 12. 4 boneless skinless chicken breasts (about 1 pound), about 1/2-inch thick; Salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste; 2 tablespoons oli…

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Step 1. Pound chicken breasts to about a 1/2-inch thickness, then season with salt and pepper.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Step 2. Heat 1 1/2 tablespoons olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Step 3. Add chicken to the hot oil and cook for 5 to 6 minutes per side, or until cooked through and no longer pink. Use an Instant Read Thermometer; chicken…

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 4. Set skillet back over medium-high heat and add the remaining oil.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Step 5. Stir in chopped shallots and garlic; cook for 1 minute.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step 6. Gradually add chicken broth; stir and scrape up all the browned bits from the bottom of the skillet.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Step 7. Bring mixture to a boil; continue to boil gently for 10 minutes, or until liquid is reduced to about 1/3 cup.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Step 8. Reduce heat to medium and whisk in the heavy cream.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Step 9. Add butter a few cubes at a time, stirring after every addition until butter melts.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Step 10. Stir in 1 tablespoon chopped fresh cilantro, chopped chile pepper, and adobo sauce.

13
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Step 11. Taste the sauce for salt and pepper, and adjust accordingly.

14
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Step 12. Add the chicken back into the pan; cook for 1 minute, or just enough to heat through.

15
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.000
You're ready. Use Make It for checkboxes on the page.
